---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title       = 'Do Ravens Migrate?';
const description = 'Most Common Ravens are non-migratory residents, but some northern populations do move south in winter. This page explains which populations move, how far, and why.';
const path        = '/questions/do-ravens-migrate/';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home',      url: '/' },
  { name: 'Questions', url: '/questions/' },
  { name: 'Do Ravens Migrate?', url: path },
];

const faq = [
  { q: 'Are ravens migratory birds?', a: 'Most Common Ravens are resident (non-migratory). Breeding pairs typically remain on or near their territory year-round. Some young, non-breeding ravens in high-latitude populations (Alaska, northern Canada, Siberia) move south in winter, but this is a partial, facultative movement rather than a fixed annual migration.' },
  { q: 'Do ravens in the UK migrate?', a: 'No. Common Ravens in the UK are year-round residents. They do not migrate. After legal protection, the UK population has expanded but remains resident throughout the year in Wales, Scotland, Ireland, and the uplands of northern England.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} ogType="article"
  datePublished="2026-11-07" dateModified="2026-11-07"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} faq={faq} pageType="Article">

<article class="qa-page">
  <nav class="qa-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol>
      {breadcrumbs.map((b, i) => (
        <li>
          {i < breadcrumbs.length - 1
            ? <><a href={b.url}>{b.name}</a><span aria-hidden="true"> › </span></>
            : <span aria-current="page">{b.name}</span>}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </nav>
  <header class="qa-header">
    <p class="qa-pillar">Question · Biology</p>
    <h1>Do Ravens Migrate?</h1>
  </header>
  <section class="qa-snippet" aria-label="Direct answer">
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> Most Common Ravens do not migrate — they are year-round residents on or near their breeding territories. However, young, non-breeding birds in the highest-latitude populations (Alaska, northern Canada, northernmost Scandinavia) may move south in winter when food becomes scarce. This is a partial, facultative movement — triggered by food shortage — not a fixed annual migration like that of warblers or geese.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Resident Pairs vs Nomadic Non-Breeders</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> There is an important distinction between two raven life stages:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Breeding adults:</strong> once a pair holds a territory, they typically remain on it year-round, defending it against other ravens and other corvids. These birds do not migrate.</li>
      <li><strong>Non-breeding floaters:</strong> young ravens (1–3 years old) that have not yet established a territory roam widely in search of food, often joining communal roosts. These birds may show seasonal movements, travelling further south in winter in northern latitudes.<sup><a href="#src-1">1</a></sup></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>High-Latitude Movements</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> In Alaska and northern Canada, some Common Ravens move to lower latitudes or coastal areas in mid-winter when snow and ice cover reduces food availability. Ringing (banding) studies show these movements can cover hundreds of kilometres, but they are not predictable year-on-year and do not involve the entire population.<sup><a href="#src-1">1</a></sup></p>
  </section>
  <section class="qa-faq qa-section" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <h2 id="faq-h2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    {faq.map(item => (
      <details class="qa-faq-item">
        <summary class="qa-faq-q">{item.q}</summary>
        <p class="qa-faq-a">{item.a}</p>
      </details>
    ))}
  </section>
  <section class="qa-sources qa-section" aria-labelledby="src-h2">
    <h2 id="src-h2">Sources</h2>
    <ol class="qa-src-list">
      <li id="src-1">Boarman, W.I. & Heinrich, B. (1999). Common Raven (<em>Corvus corax</em>). <em>Birds of the World</em>. Cornell Lab. — resident behaviour, partial movements.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="qa-claim-note"><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> peer-reviewed/field-guide data</p>
  </section>
</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .qa-page { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem; color: var(--iron-ink, #e8e4d8); font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; line-height: 1.72; }
  .qa-breadcrumb ol { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .25rem; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--ink-soft, #8a8070); }
  .qa-breadcrumb a { color: var(--gold-500, #d4ae5a); text-decoration: none; }
  .qa-pillar { font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold-500, #d4ae5a); margin: 0 0 .4rem; }
  .qa-page h1 { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 2rem; line-height: 1.1; }
  .qa-snippet { background: rgba(212,174,90,.08); border-left: 3px solid var(--gold-500, #d4ae5a); border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.03rem; }
  .qa-section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .qa-section h2 { font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 .9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(212,174,90,.2); padding-bottom: .4rem; }
  .qa-section p { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: .97rem; }
  .qa-section ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .qa-section li { margin-bottom: .4rem; font-size: .95rem; }
  .claim-science { color: #7ab9e0; font-style: normal; font-size: .78rem; }
  a[href] { color: var(--gold-500, #d4ae5a); }
  .qa-faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07); }
  .qa-faq-q { cursor: pointer; padding: .9rem 0; font-size: .97rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; list-style: none; }
  .qa-faq-q::before { content: '+ '; color: var(--gold-500, #d4ae5a); font-weight: 700; }
  details[open] .qa-faq-q::before { content: '− '; }
  .qa-faq-a { margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.7; font-size: .93rem; color: var(--ink-soft, #c8c0b0); }
  .qa-src-list { padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .qa-src-list li { margin-bottom: .6rem; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--ink-soft, #8a8070); line-height: 1.6; }
  .qa-claim-note { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--ink-soft, #605848); border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06); padding-top: .75rem; }
</style>
